.TH SCAN_PB_TYPE1_FIXED64 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
scan_pb_type1_fixed64 \- Scan a Protocol Buffers fixed 64-bit integer type 1 from a string

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/scan.h>
.IB #include <lib/uint64.h>

.IB size_t
.IB scan_pb_type1_fixed64(const char* in, size_t len, uint64* d);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBscan_pb_type1_fixed64\fR function scans a Protocol Buffers fixed 64-bit integer type 1 from a given string and stores the result.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB in
The input string containing the Protocol Buffers fixed 64-bit integer type 1.
.TP
.IB len
The length of the input string.
.TP
.IB d
The destination where the scanned fixed 64-bit integer will be stored.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the number of characters processed.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBscan_pb_type1_fixed64\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/scan.h>
#include <lib/uint64.h>

int main() {
    const char* fixed64 = "\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x01";
    uint64 result;
    size_t length = scan_pb_type1_fixed64(fixed64, 8, &result);
    printf("Scanned fixed 64-bit integer: %llu\n", result);
    printf("Length processed: %zu\n", length);
    return 0;
}
.nef